              "textField": "Some of the long term side effects of greatly reducing the stomach acids with medications like famotidine and other Histamine 2 receptor blockers and Omeprazole and other proton pump inhibitors include increased risk of *osteoporosis* due to reduction of *magnesium* and calcium from the GIT. There is also an increased risk of *Vitamin B12* deficiencies, which can lead to a type of dementia. The client taking these may have an increased risk of *Respiratory infections* as well."
